-- title:
--   Split tori and reflection normalizers in PSL₂ over finite fields
-- statement:
--   Let F be a finite field of cardinality p^f with p prime, and set d=gcd(|F|-1,2). There is a cyclic subgroup U of PSL₂(F) of order (|F|-1)/d and an involution w outside U which normalizes U and acts on U by inversion. The subgroup generated by U and w has order 2|U|. Every nontrivial subgroup R of U has normalizer exactly that generated subgroup. This retains the reflection data of Huppert II.8.3.
